-- title:
--   Existence of a product-measure datum with prescribed ord and S-part
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, equip its idele group $(\mathbb{A}_K^\times) = (\mathrm{AdeleRing}(\mathcal{O}_K,K))^\times$ with a measurable structure that is the Borel structure of its topology, let $S$ be a finite set of height-one primes of $\mathcal{O}_K$, and let $\nu$ be a Haar measure on the idele group. Then there exists a datum $P$ of type [`UnramifiedWhittaker.ProductMeasureData`](def/UnramifiedWhittaker_ZetaIntegrand.html#L20) for $(S,\nu)$ — that is, a real constant $c>0$, a measure $\nu_S$ on the ideles, a monoid endomorphism $\mathrm{proj}_S$ of the ideles, and a function $\mathrm{ord}$ assigning to a prime $v$ and an idele an integer, subject to: the finite component of $\mathrm{proj}_S a$ at each $v\notin S$ equals $1$; for every repetition-free list $L$ of primes outside $S$, every idele $a$ that is a unit at all finite places outside $S\cup L$ factors as $\mathrm{proj}_S a$ times $\prod_{v\in L}\pi_v^{\mathrm{ord}_v a}$ (with $\pi_v$ the idele `uniformizerIdele`) times an idele with trivial archimedean part, trivial components at the places of $S$, and integral finite part with integral inverse; the corresponding sets of ideles are measurable; and the Tonelli-type identity holds, namely for $f$ integrable for $\nu_S$ and $\varphi_v$ absolutely summable on $\mathbb{Z}$ the function $a\mapsto f(\mathrm{proj}_S a)\prod_{v\in L}\varphi_v(\mathrm{ord}_v a)$ is $\nu$-integrable over that set with integral $c\,(\int f\,d\nu_S)\prod_{v\in L}\sum_{m\in\mathbb{Z}}\varphi_v(m)$ — such that moreover $P.\mathrm{ord}$ is the standard profile $\mathrm{ord}_v(a)=-\log$ of the valuation of the $v$-component of $a$, $P.\mathrm{proj}_S$ is [`NumberField.Idele.partAt K SK`](def/NumberField_IdeleProductMeasure.html#L90) (identity on the archimedean component, `truncFin` on the finite part), and $\mathrm{ofReal}(P.c)\cdot P.\nu_S$ equals the pushforward along `partAt K SK` of the restriction of $\nu$ to the subgroup of ideles that are units at every finite place outside $S$.
--
--   This supplies, for an arbitrary Haar measure on the idele group, the product-measure datum packaging the decomposition of the idele group into its $S$-part and the free abelian group generated by uniformisers outside $S$, together with the resulting term-by-term unfolding of integrals into Euler-type products. It is used to discharge the corresponding hypothesis in the theorems on winding data relating Hecke-word class integrals to Satake Laurent expansions.
